WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.270
Speaker 1: Welcome to the show.

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:02.590
It's great to be back.

00:00:02.590 --> 00:00:07.189
I know I'm tan, please, no emails about me
being tan.

00:00:07.189 --> 00:00:09.980
I wore sunscreen, I did all of it.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:16.250
We had a lot of major, major news events during
the period that I was gone.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:20.990
Farin and Jesse did a really great job of
staying on top of everything for you.

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:27.520
And I want to start today with the most requested
segment over the last 72 hours, which was

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:33.150
people coming to me and saying, David, sir,
please tell us what you think about what's

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:35.310
going on in Afghanistan now.

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:39.691
As many of you who have been with the show
for a while may remember, you may not, but

00:00:39.691 --> 00:00:42.590
you may that we'll find out soon.

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:48.500
You might remember that I talked about the
Afghanistan withdrawal when Donald Trump planned

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:51.510
to do it and announced that he was doing it.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:55.230
And I talked about it again when Joe Biden
announced, hey, that pause we put on Trump's

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:56.750
Afghanistan withdrawal.

00:00:56.750 --> 00:00:59.620
We've evaluated it and we are going to do
it.

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:02.780
And it's going to happen by September 11th.

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:08.830
President Joe Biden is now being widely criticized
for his actions in Afghanistan, which are

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:16.260
carrying out the plan to remove troops that
Donald Trump and Republicans bragged about

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:21.550
and cheered for for months during the end
of Donald Trump's presidency.

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:26.920
Now, that's not me starting to say, well,
I'm going to blame here or there.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.260
It's just the reality.

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:33.930
What Biden did was to go forward with more
or less the plan that Donald Trump announced

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:40.900
and that Trump cheered and that Trump cheered
predictably, just like we said a few months

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:46.470
ago, whether it was Trump leaving or Biden
leaving, it would cause chaos.

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:52.430
But at a certain point, our responsibility
has to end because our involvement has been

00:01:52.430 --> 00:01:53.760
a disaster.

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:56.030
Staying longer won't solve anything.

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:58.290
The Afghanistan intervention failed.

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:02.290
And it's really important in these cases when
people start saying, oh, we left the wrong

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:06.290
way or we did, OK, we can talk about that.

00:02:06.290 --> 00:02:09.929
But at a certain point, our involvement had
to end.

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:14.620
Even though Biden is sending 6000 troops back
in now, which we'll get to.

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:17.340
And it was going to be a fiasco whenever it
ended.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:22.940
Those things were essentially the they were
certain, regardless of which president was

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:27.510
in the Oval Office when this happened, so
we could stay and keep failing or we could

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:33.550
leave the vacuum when we left, as was worldwide
news earlier this week, immediately led to

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:38.560
the Taliban taking over and then all sorts
of different hot takes.

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:40.990
Joe Biden left the wrong way.

00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:47.150
We do have to ensure the safety of our people
and to be empathetic when it comes to refugees

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:56.240
that we I am on board by saying there should
have been better advance action to prevent

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:59.200
some of what we saw there.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:03.980
But unfortunately, a lot of it was essentially
inevitable.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:10.530
As we said months ago, the same people, pro
Trump Republicans who now are ignoring that

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:17.340
Donald Trump had the same plan, are starting
to say this would have been totally different

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:19.840
if it had been managed by a different president.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:22.240
Actually, no, it wouldn't have been.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:26.989
And there are some Trump acts as well as people
on the left who just don't like Joe Biden,

00:03:26.989 --> 00:03:32.130
who are now saying, well, the vacuum allowed
the Taliban to take over and we didn't do

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:36.580
enough to get our people, other people, refugees
out in time.

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:41.470
If we had done the get people out in time
part, do you think those people would be satisfied?

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:47.640
No, those very same people would just be focusing
on the Taliban took over and we would be seeing

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:50.879
the exact same reactions from those people.

00:03:50.879 --> 00:03:55.810
And sadly, there are tons of bad faith actors
on both sides on this issue.

00:03:55.810 --> 00:04:00.080
Now, I'm not saying the same number of people
on both sides.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:04.269
I would be called out for playing the both
sides game if I did that.

00:04:04.269 --> 00:04:07.280
But there are bad faith actors on both sides
right now.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:12.220
You have people on the right saying terrible
decision by Joe Biden when Trump was going

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:15.140
to do this, it was going to be totally different.

00:04:15.140 --> 00:04:17.269
No, Trump would have done it in the exact
same way.

00:04:17.269 --> 00:04:21.529
Don't let them lie and say Trump had some
master plan for preventing what happened.

00:04:21.529 --> 00:04:23.139
Trump had no master plan for anything.

00:04:23.139 --> 00:04:27.900
The idea that he would have had such a plan
for Afghanistan is absolutely absurd.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.129
Trump would have done the exact same thing.

00:04:30.129 --> 00:04:32.181
And by the way.

00:04:32.181 --> 00:04:39.419
All the references to this being Trump's plan
all along suddenly removed from the GOP website,

00:04:39.419 --> 00:04:43.860
Trump's websites within hours of this going
down in Afghanistan, all of those references

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:48.039
to Trump's plan to get out of Afghanistan,
deal with the Taliban, etc.

00:04:48.039 --> 00:04:52.419
It's a bold faced attempt to revise history.

00:04:52.419 --> 00:04:58.879
Then the left saying this is the typical centrist
Democrat foreign policy of Joe Biden.

00:04:58.879 --> 00:05:01.259
You go in for the wrong reasons and then you
cut and run.

00:05:01.259 --> 00:05:02.300
Well, hold on a second.

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:08.490
George W. Bush is responsible for us being
there, not Joe Biden, not Donald Trump and

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:09.919
not Barack Obama.

00:05:09.919 --> 00:05:13.300
There is not nearly enough discussion of George
W. Bush here.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:18.710
And I think that, you know, if you go to a
bad dentist and the dentist screws up your

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:20.310
tooth.

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:25.189
And then you go to other dentists and the
first dentist that tries to fix it doesn't

00:05:25.189 --> 00:05:30.229
do a great job, and then you go to a third
dentist and that dentist basically gets you

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:31.729
out of harm's way.

00:05:31.729 --> 00:05:35.469
You're not going to have an abscess, but the
tooth is going to hurt for several months.

00:05:35.469 --> 00:05:39.259
We talk about what the third dentist wasn't
able to do.

00:05:39.259 --> 00:05:42.560
We talk about how the second dentist messed
up the repair.

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:46.339
But what started it was that first dentist
who messed up your tooth.

00:05:46.339 --> 00:05:51.740
And there is not nearly enough discussion
to use a dental analogy of George W. Bush

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:53.499
in the Bush administration's role here.

00:05:53.499 --> 00:05:55.849
There's a lot of Biden versus Trump stuff.

00:05:55.849 --> 00:06:02.289
At some point, someone had to say what George
W. Bush started can go no further, no more

00:06:02.289 --> 00:06:03.919
money into this.

00:06:03.919 --> 00:06:05.720
No more contractors getting rich.

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:09.330
The contractors mostly out of Afghanistan
over recent months because the withdrawal

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:12.590
was coming that with the contractors.

00:06:12.590 --> 00:06:14.919
We've got to stop that as well.

00:06:14.919 --> 00:06:19.660
And Joe Biden's speech to the nation on Monday,
it wasn't satisfying to a lot of people who

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:24.270
emailed me, but it was fundamentally an honest
speech.

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:28.680
And by honest, I mean, it's the type of honesty
we don't usually get from politicians.

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:33.089
It was one of the most honest political speeches
by a president in a long time.

00:06:33.089 --> 00:06:34.819
And it was completely decisive.

00:06:34.819 --> 00:06:37.240
It was we had to do it.

00:06:37.240 --> 00:06:38.240
We had to do it.

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:43.669
As I tweeted earlier this week, quote, So
you stay another year to leave correctly,

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:49.480
simply delaying what happened by a year, enriching
more contractors who would go back in.

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:51.659
And so then what?

00:06:51.659 --> 00:06:54.740
The same thing happens in 2022.

00:06:54.740 --> 00:06:57.589
At some point you have to cut your losses.

00:06:57.589 --> 00:07:01.710
And Joe Biden's speech was decisive and Joe
Biden was the guy to do it.

00:07:01.710 --> 00:07:04.199
And he takes responsibility for what took
place after.

00:07:04.199 --> 00:07:08.780
Now, if there is anything to really criticize
there, it's well, now 6000 troops are going

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:15.710
back in to help people get out and restabilize,
which we could say is going backwards.

00:07:15.710 --> 00:07:21.870
You pull out the last fifteen hundred chaos
ensues and you sends that 6000 back in.

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:29.550
So I'm not saying it's wrong to try to help
grease the exit in some way.

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:30.969
That's not my criticism.

00:07:30.969 --> 00:07:33.879
But in a sense, are we really even doing it?

00:07:33.879 --> 00:07:38.311
If 6000 are going back and the devil really
is in the details with what those 6000 are

00:07:38.311 --> 00:07:43.999
going to be doing and we will get back and
we'll dig into that further probably later

00:07:43.999 --> 00:07:44.999
this week.

00:07:44.999 --> 00:07:45.999
But you know what?

00:07:45.999 --> 00:07:47.149
It had to be done.

00:07:47.149 --> 00:07:53.800
You don't tend to see this level of decisive
action on foreign policy combined with just

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:55.889
telling it like it is.

00:07:55.889 --> 00:07:59.819
And so I think for that, you have to give
Biden credit and then we figure out which

00:07:59.819 --> 00:08:27.009
aspects of it could have been better managed.

00:08:27.009 --> 00:08:27.270
I

